# G2: exactness of the levers, strictly. The S3a matrix plan on c2-packed-tp4-gate-vglue (all five levers on, QWEN_FAST_TP4_VGLUE_AUDIT=1
# and every audit the gate profile carries): four real-text users at 4,096 / 16,384 / 32,768 / 60,000 tokens, 512 tokens out, a
# concurrent arm (all four at once: packed-4 rounds, users 2 and 3 in rows 32-63 of the 64-row block) and a solo arm (the same
# prompts one at a time: the sequential engine, one tile), strict policy: every concurrent text must equal its solo text. The
# prompts are the image's own real-text corpus by (user index, length), so they are the S3a prompts: the SOLO texts must equal
# S3a's offline (the solo engine never takes a lever), and the concurrent texts must equal S3a's concurrent texts (the levers are
# byte-identical replacements: any difference from S3a's concurrent texts is a lever defect).
# In-trace, every round (every layer on round 1, then two per round in rotation, verify_trace_t2.audit_layers): beside each lever the
# served path is built and held, and packed_verifier compares after the replay, on every chip, as int16 bit patterns: the GDN
# pieces (users 1 and 3 canonical), the merged output and its placement, per user conv / beta / g / z and every advanced window,
# and the sampler's gathered maxima against ttnn.max. The first round compares all 48 layers. Expected audit line:
# '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue audit N exact=True layers=0-47 entries=<48 x (4 pieces + 1 merge + 32 block)>' then '... layers=a,b entries=...'.
# What this cannot show is the one thing the unit tests cannot: that the untilize / tilize round trip and the conv-gates op really
# are the value rules the levers emulate (zero exponent -> +0; a row's result independent of its tile row and face). An audit
# mismatch names the lever, the layer, the user and the element count. The edge probe (injected -0 and denormal rows) is a separate
# one-card job, not part of this window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card verify-glue window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/vglue and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image G0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-vglue-1 is a PLACEHOLDER: set it (in every template of the window) to the tag the driver of the window picks, once
# the image is built from the pushed branch.
# C2_GATE_JIT=record: the kernel cache holds no entry for the new launches, so the first arm compiles them; the growth is recorded, not judged.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; per arm one engine build 10-30 min plus 6-16 min of streams (the audit copies and replays every
# audited layer): two arms 40-90 min; a reproduced divergence re-runs both arms once: up to 170 min.
# STOP on the gate exit (strict): any concurrent text differing from its solo text fails the job, and so does an audit mismatch.
# Read: the gate verdict per arm; per user IDENTICAL concurrent against solo; the vglue audit lines (every one exact=True, none
# mismatch); the vglue markers (engaged counts; no fell-back line); the extent, T1 and T2 audits clean; zero refusals; the [ACCEPT]
# line; the divergence records file if any user differs. Then offline: the SOLO texts against S3a's solo texts (byte identical), the
# CONCURRENT texts against S3a's concurrent texts (byte identical).
# Proves: concurrent (packed, levers on) equals solo (sequential) for all four users on real text, and each lever's output equals the
# served path's bit for bit on every audited layer.
# The markers to read (scripts/ci/tp4_vglue.py): '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue engaged site=packed_verify levers=<list> attn_fold=16
# gdn_glue=48 gdn_merge=48 gdn_block_conv=48 shard_values=1' once per captured verify trace (the counts are per layer: 16 attention
# layers, 48 GDN layers; a lever that fell back shows its own *_fallback count instead), '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue engaged site=commit
# lanes=<workers per layer x layers> chips=4' once, and '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue engaged site=sampler shard_values=1' once.
# '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue fell back site=<split|merge|block_conv|attention|sampler> reason=...' is a lever declining (its served path
# ran instead): read every one before trusting a timing, because a fallen-back lever saves nothing. Any '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue audit
# mismatch' line fails the smoke and the gate by itself (c2_smoke_check's 'audit mismatch' rule).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-vglue-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate-vglue
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=4096,16384,32768,60000
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=512
C2_GATE_JIT=record
